{"id": "tea:vajasaneyi-samhita:40.15-17", "source": "src:vajasaneyi-samhita", "location": {"ref": "40.15-17", "chapter": "40", "verse": "15-17", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "At the close of the Mādhyandina Saṃhitā: 'Oṃ, intent (kratu), remember; remember what was done'; 'Agni, lead us by the good path'; 'the face of truth is covered with a golden vessel; the Person who is in the sun, he am I; Oṃ, the void (kha) is brahman'.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "sound"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "death-dying", "sound-language"], "terms": ["trm:om", "trm:brahman", "trm:purusa", "trm:satya", "trm:kratu"], "concepts": ["cpt:brahman-early-sense"], "notes": "Checked in the local VS text. VS 40 is the Mādhyandina form of the Īśa Upaniṣad (U03 owns src:isa-upanisad); recorded here for its Saṃhitā wording.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked", "checked_by": null, "date": null, "note": ""}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U01-vedic-samhitas"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U01-vedic-samhitas"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
